          ":question/id": "9b98c70c-6a88-51cb-9877-b27cf2c2def7",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-110510",
          ":question/problem": "Find the slope of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=-7arccscx$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7arccscx) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{7}{|\\sqrt{5}|\\sqrt{{\\sqrt{5}}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
