              ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"
