              ":question/id": "99db3f5c-5d6f-5e8e-a31c-a627ddd5c6dc",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-208",
              ":question/problem": "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec } x}{\\textrm{arccsc } x},$ calculate $f'(x).$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we let $u(x) = \\textrm{arcsec } x$ and $v(x) = \\textrm{arccsc } x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) =  \\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\t\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\tv'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\text{arccsc }x-\\text{arcsec }x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}{\\text{ arccsc }}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"
