              ":question/problem": "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) =2 \\, \\textrm {arccot } (x^2 + 5).$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }({x}^{2}+5)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+26}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
